WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.008
Stop thinking and start doing.

00:00:06.008 --> 00:00:09.314
One of my favorite stories is of Mary Kay Ash.

00:00:09.314 --> 00:00:13.231
She was a successful entrepreneur, founder of Mary Kay cosmetics.

00:00:13.231 --> 00:00:18.247
Her life changed when she was a young mother and her husband came back from the war and...

00:00:18.247 --> 00:00:20.298
ran off with another woman.

00:00:20.298 --> 00:00:26.120
And she now had to find a way to support the family, so she joined up with a direct sales company...

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.051
and was selling things door to door.

00:00:28.051 --> 00:00:34.762
And she quickly became the #1 salesperson at the business, but she was passed over on...

00:00:34.762 --> 00:00:37.983
opportunities for promotion because she was a woman.

00:00:37.983 --> 00:00:44.413
She kept seeing men with less experience, less success, be promoted ahead of her.

00:00:44.413 --> 00:00:46.717
So she said: "I'm tired of this! I'm not going to do this anymore!...

00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:48.458
I´m going to go find another company!"

00:00:48.458 --> 00:00:52.068
So she hooked up with a different direct sales company, she brought her experience there and, again,...

00:00:52.068 --> 00:00:54.701
she quickly became on of the top sales people there.

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:58.369
And she earned a few promotions and she even got on the board of directors.

00:00:58.369 --> 00:01:02.435
But she kept getting put down because she was a woman.

00:01:02.435 --> 00:01:06.331
Her ideas would be ignored and the board would frequently tell her:

00:01:06.331 --> 00:01:09.159
"Oh, Mary Kay, you're just thinking like a woman."

00:01:09.159 --> 00:01:12.607
A comment that constantly infuriated her.

00:01:12.607 --> 00:01:21.033
She got so frustrated and her breaking point came when one of the guys that she trained, for years at the...

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:27.889
business, was promoted to be her boss and paid twice her salary. And she said:

00:01:27.889 --> 00:01:33.023
"That's it. I'm done! I can't handle these companies, I'm not being respected,...

00:01:33.023 --> 00:01:37.800
I'm not being treated like I'm adding value, so I'm done!" And she quit.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.669
And she went home and said: "You know what? I'm going to write a book!"

00:01:40.669 --> 00:01:44.990
"I'm going to write a book and I'm going to talk about all the reasons why corporate America is wrong...

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:48.653
right now. And how women are being passed over and how this isn't right!"

00:01:48.653 --> 00:01:54.112
"And then I'm also going to include a section on what an ideal company should look like."

00:01:54.112 --> 00:01:57.340
"How people would be treated with respect and how business should be run."

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:03.747
And then the turning point came. She said: "Instead of just thinking about it, instead of just writing about it,...

00:02:03.747 --> 00:02:10.615
"I'm going to go do it! I'm going to launch my own business that would be the ideal company to work for."

00:02:10.615 --> 00:02:16.289
And she turned all the negative things that happened to her in her life, how she was passed over repeatedly...

00:02:16.289 --> 00:02:18.625
and being put down for being a woman.

00:02:18.625 --> 00:02:22.722
She took all that negative energy and turned it into something amazingly positive.

00:02:22.722 --> 00:02:30.002
And took an idea from nothing, from scratch, just an idea, into a billion dollar plus company.

00:02:30.002 --> 00:02:35.553
And when she was asked: "What do you think your legacy is going to be?", she said:

00:02:35.553 --> 00:02:42.384
"I think the biggest legacy we're going to leave is a whole community of children who believe they can do anything...

00:02:42.384 --> 00:02:45.554
in this world because they watched their mommas do it."

00:02:45.554 --> 00:02:50.450
So stop thinking about it, stop writing about it and start doing.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:51.988
Believe!

